-- The condition 100 NOT IN (200) is true so Q1 returns {100}.

-- Q2: The LEFT JOIN filtered by P.c4 = 'S8' yields the same S8 row (c1 = 100) and the subquery also returns (200), thus 100 passes (since 100 is not equal to 200) so Q2 returns {100}.

-- In any data set obeying the constraints, these two queries end up behaving the same, so no counterexample exists.

