-- There is no counterexample in this schema. However, here is one sample test dataset illustrating that both queries yield the same result:

INSERT INTO table1 (c1) VALUES (1);
INSERT INTO table1 (c1) VALUES (3);
INSERT INTO table1 (c1) VALUES (7);

-- For this data, Q1 computes MIN(ABS(3-1), ABS(7-1), ABS(7-3)) = MIN(2,6,4) = 2
-- and Q2 (when ordering the values as 1,3,7) computes differences 3-1 = 2 and 7-3 = 4, with MIN = 2
-- Therefore, both queries return 2.  

-- Since the schema forbids duplicate c1 values and all c1 values are non‐NULL, no valid counterexample (where the results differ) exists.

